(HKMA Supervisory Policy Manual SA-2: Capital Adequacy Requirements) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Hong Kong Monetary Authority) Tj
T*
(Supervisory Policy Manual) Tj
T*
(SA-2: Capital Adequacy Requirements) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Introduction) Tj
T*
(The Hong Kong Monetary Authority \(HKMA\) requires all authorized institutions to maintain) Tj
T*
(adequate capital to support their risk profile and business activities. This policy) Tj
T*
(manual outlines the minimum capital adequacy requirements for banks operating in Hong) Tj
T*
(Kong.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Minimum Capital Requirements) Tj
T*
(2.1 Common Equity Tier 1 \(CET1\) Capital Ratio) Tj
T*
(Authorized institutions must maintain a minimum Common Equity Tier 1 capital ratio of) Tj
T*
(4.5% of risk-weighted assets. This requirement aligns with the Basel III international) Tj
T*
(standard.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.2 Tier 1 Capital Ratio) Tj
T*
(The minimum Tier 1 capital ratio is set at 6.0% of risk-weighted assets. Tier 1 capital) Tj
T*
(consists of CET1 capital and Additional Tier 1 capital instruments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.3 Total Capital Ratio) Tj
T*
(Banks must maintain a minimum total capital ratio of 8.0% of risk-weighted assets. Total) Tj
T*
(capital includes Tier 1 capital and Tier 2 capital.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Capital Conservation Buffer) Tj
T*
(3.1 Buffer Requirement) Tj
T*
(Authorized institutions are required to maintain a capital conservation buffer of 2.5%) Tj
T*
(of risk-weighted assets, comprising Common Equity Tier 1 capital.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 Buffer Purpose) Tj
T*
(The buffer is designed to ensure that banks build up capital buffers outside periods of) Tj
T*
(stress which can be drawn down as losses are incurred.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Countercyclical Capital Buffer) Tj
T*
(4.1 Variable Buffer) Tj
T*
(The HKMA may activate a countercyclical capital buffer ranging from 0% to 2.5% of) Tj
T*
(risk-weighted assets, depending on credit conditions in Hong Kong.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 Implementation) Tj
T*
(The countercyclical buffer is implemented in accordance with Basel III standards and) Tj
T*
(HKMA's assessment of systemic risk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Leverage Ratio) Tj
T*
(5.1 Minimum Requirement) Tj
T*
(Banks must maintain a minimum leverage ratio of 3% of total exposures. The leverage) Tj
T*
(ratio is a non-risk-based measure that supplements risk-based capital requirements.) Tj
ET
